// @error-at 3:11 `downTo` is not a range keyword — a descending range is `to` with a negative step: `for i in hi to lo step -1`
// diderven DV-800 — Kotlin's `downTo` drew four errors (braces, for-in over i32, two undeclared
// names). It is one refusal naming VL's spelling; the rest of the loop parses as a `to` range.
for i in 5 downTo 0 { print(i) }
